From 8f054f19fdcfc3bf795353ac73b861b9984eb32d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:49:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 232/638] chrome: report AROS browser process details
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Chrome memory reporting selected no AROS implementation and generic POSIX code classified processes through the Linux zygote host; the extension CPU API likewise had no AROS per-core time provider.

FIX_REASON: Enumerate the current browser task and Chrome-known child tasks using portable process data, retain Chromium memory-instrumentation footprint collection, exclude the absent Linux zygote, and report per-core time as unavailable until task.resource exposes a stable accounting API.

SCOPE: chrome/browser memory details and extensions system CPU AROS platform sources.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-chrome -j48 obj/chrome/browser/libbrowser.a extensions/browser/api/system_cpu:system_cpu

RISK: AROS-wide process discovery and cumulative per-core CPU time remain unavailable; reported task identity and browser-child classification are real.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
